sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Caller
    participant Twilio
    participant Edge as WAF / Load balancer
    participant App as Your app
    participant Store as Replay store

    Caller->>Twilio: Dials your number
    Twilio->>Edge: POST /voice (X-Twilio-Signature)
    Edge->>App: forwarded

    rect rgb(254, 246, 228)
        Note over App: Enforcement point 1 — HTTP webhook
        App->>App: Validate signature over https:// URL
        App->>App: Mint token bound to CallSid (90s TTL)
    end

    App-->>Twilio: TwiML #lt;ConversationRelay url="wss://…?t=JWT"#gt;

    Twilio->>Edge: HTTP Upgrade + X-Twilio-Signature
    Note over Edge: The ONLY hop the WAF can inspect
    Edge->>App: forwarded upgrade request

    rect rgb(254, 246, 228)
        Note over App: Enforcement point 2 — the handshake
        App->>App: 1. Validate signature over wss:// URL
        App->>Store: 2. Claim jti (atomic, single-use)
        Store-->>App: first use? yes / no
    end

    alt Any check fails
        App-->>Twilio: 401 — no 101, no session allocated
        Note over Caller,App: Connection never exists
    else All checks pass
        App-->>Twilio: 101 Switching Protocols
        Twilio->>App: setup { callSid, from, to }
        App->>App: 3. Assert setup.callSid == token claim
        Note over Edge: Every frame from here on is<br/>invisible to the WAF
        Twilio->>App: prompt { voicePrompt } — untrusted input
        App-->>Twilio: text { token, last }
    end
